# Third-party material and non-code assets

W Linux as a whole is licensed **GPL-3.0-or-later** — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).
That covers every script, configuration file, QML source and installer module in
this tree.

This file records the parts that are **not** original W code, or that are not
code at all, together with where they came from and under what terms. It is the
authoritative provenance record: anything shipped in `rootfs/` or `archiso/`
that W did not author from scratch is listed here.

---

## Vendored third-party code

### `rootfs/usr/lib/w/papirus-folders`

- **Upstream:** <https://github.com/PapirusDevelopmentTeam/papirus-folders>
- **Author:** Sergei Eremenko (<https://github.com/SmartFinn>)
- **License:** MIT
- **Why vendored:** W recolours Papirus folder icons from the active theme
  (`w-style`), and the upstream helper is not packaged in the Arch repositories.
  Shipped verbatim; the MIT notice stays in the file header.

MIT is GPL-3.0-compatible, so redistributing it inside a GPL-3.0-or-later work
is permitted. The MIT terms continue to govern this file on its own.

### `archiso/profile/syslinux/splash.png`

- **Upstream:** `archiso` (Arch Linux), `configs/releng/syslinux/splash.png`
- **License:** GPL-3.0-or-later
- **Note:** byte-identical to upstream. Part of the archiso profile W builds on.

---

## Derived artwork

### Kvantum widget theme

Files:

- `rootfs/etc/w/themes/w/kvantum/default.svg`
- `rootfs/etc/skel/.config/Kvantum/w/w.svg`

- **Derived from:** `KvFlat` — a theme bundled with Kvantum
  (<https://github.com/tsujan/Kvantum>), by Pedram Pourang (Tsu Jan)
- **Upstream license:** GPL-3.0-or-later
- **What W changed:** colours only. The geometry is upstream's; `w-style`
  re-tokenises the palette from `W_QT_*` at render time
  (see `kvconfig-map.conf` / `svg-map.conf`).
- **Status:** a derivative work of GPL-3.0-or-later material, therefore
  distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later like the rest of this repository.

The accompanying `default.kvconfig` (geometry and behaviour) is W's own work
and is likewise GPL-3.0-or-later.

---

## W's own artwork

Authored for W by tarkh, licensed **CC BY-SA 4.0**
(<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>):

- `rootfs/etc/w/themes/w/logo/W-logo.svg`, `W-logo-256x256.png` — the W mark
- `rootfs/etc/w/themes/w/wallpaper/*.webp`, `preview.webp` — the default
  wallpaper of theme `w`, in the four shipped resolutions plus its thumbnail
- `rootfs/usr/share/plymouth/themes/w/*.png` — boot splash bar, bullet, lock
- `rootfs/boot/grub/themes/w/select/*.png` — GRUB selection frame (9-slice)

Verified as original: none of these match any asset shipped by Plymouth, GRUB or
Kvantum on a stock Arch system.

The wallpaper was drawn for W from scratch, to the palette already in
`themes/w/theme.conf` rather than the other way round — so it carries no upstream
image and `theme.conf` is unchanged by it. It replaces an earlier wallpaper that
was derived from a downloaded photograph whose licence was never established.
That one shipped in the pre-release snapshots v0.1.1–v0.1.5 of the throwaway test
repository and nowhere else; it is gone from this tree, and the production
repository — which has not been published yet — never carried it.

---

## Test fixtures

`scripts/check/tests/fixtures/palette/matugen-*.json` are recorded outputs of
`matugen` runs, kept so the palette suite can assert against a frozen input.
They are generated data, not third-party material.
